events.content:
I have created a server component `app/server-time.tsx` that displays the current server timestamp. To ensure dynamic rendering on every request without relying on headers or cookies, I used the `connection()` function from `next/server`, which is the recommended approach in modern Next.js (App Router) for opting into dynamic rendering.

I also integrated this component into `app/page.tsx` and verified the implementation by running `npm run build`, which confirmed the route is treated as dynamic (`ƒ`). Additionally, I added a basic test `app/server-time.test.tsx` to verify the component renders correctly.

### Created File: `app/server-time.tsx`
```tsx
import { connection } from 'next/server';

export default async function ServerTime() {
  await connection();
  return (
    <div id="server-time">
      Current Server Time: {new Date().toISOString()}
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Updated File: `app/page.tsx`
```tsx
import ServerTime from './server-time';

export default function Home() {
  return (
    <main>
      <h1>Server Time Example</h1>
      <ServerTime />
    </main>
  );
}
```

